WEBVTT

00:01.160 --> 00:02.880
The Pokémon League of Fierce Fights!

00:01.980 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:03.890 --> 00:05.790
I'm Pachira, the show's anchor.

00:06.360 --> 00:09.460
The Kalos League has passed its halfway mark, and the second half will now begin.

00:10.370 --> 00:13.490
Now then, let's look back at the battles we've seen so far with this digest.

00:15.360 --> 00:20.000
Right from the first round, there have been developments you couldn't avert your eyes from,

00:20.380 --> 00:24.300
like the showdown between Alan and Trova's Mega Lizardon, as well as Satoshi's Gekkouga.

00:25.650 --> 00:29.680
What makes this tournament so special is, by all accounts, the mega evolving Pokémon!

00:30.400 --> 00:31.970
There's Ayaka's Mega Absol,

00:32.660 --> 00:34.420
and Louis' Mega Gablias...

00:35.220 --> 00:41.520
Due to Mega Evolutions playing such a big role, the Kalos League provides even more mega-excitement than previous years!

00:44.190 --> 00:46.330
I'm looking forward to the matches of the second half even more now!

00:47.040 --> 00:48.960
This has been a report from Pachira.

00:52.230 --> 00:57.980
Mega Jukain VS Raichu!
I Received Some EXP!!

00:58.320 --> 01:00.250
Absol, Psycho Cut!

01:02.760 --> 01:04.550
Luchabull, Flying Press!

01:14.390 --> 01:14.960
Absol!

01:15.880 --> 01:17.270
Absol is unable to battle.

01:17.640 --> 01:19.590
Therefore, the winner is Satoshi!

01:19.960 --> 01:20.800
All right!

01:21.480 --> 01:25.780
Satoshi is the second competitor to advance to the semifinals, following Alan!

01:26.980 --> 01:36.860
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:26.980 --> 01:36.860
Z

01:31.150 --> 01:31.830
Satoshi.

01:32.590 --> 01:33.340
Shota.

01:33.680 --> 01:35.940
Congratulations on making it to the semifinals.

01:36.180 --> 01:36.820
Thank you.

01:37.410 --> 01:38.820
You're up next, Shota.

01:39.310 --> 01:39.650
Yes.

01:40.310 --> 01:41.320
I will win, of course!

01:43.490 --> 01:44.070
Satoshi...

01:45.410 --> 01:46.330
Do you remember?

01:47.430 --> 01:49.080
...and fight you at the League, no matter what.

01:49.670 --> 01:51.200
I can't leave it at that loss.

01:52.690 --> 01:54.210
Let's settle this at the League!

01:57.070 --> 01:58.800
Yes, of course!

02:00.300 --> 02:01.340
That is why I will win!

02:02.050 --> 02:02.370
Sure!

02:03.510 --> 02:04.840
Tierno is strong too, though.

02:05.390 --> 02:07.010
He is an acquaintance of yours, right?

02:07.500 --> 02:07.820
Yeah.

02:09.190 --> 02:10.960
Looking at his matches in the first and second rounds,

02:11.460 --> 02:14.360
I see that I have to be cautious about his rhythm-based battling style.

02:16.990 --> 02:18.610
I will break his rhythm!

02:19.280 --> 02:20.360
I expect nothing less from you, Shota.

02:21.080 --> 02:23.080
I have done all I could.

02:24.050 --> 02:26.160
Also, I have a secret weapon.

02:26.880 --> 02:27.890
A secret weapon?

02:28.990 --> 02:30.200
It is secret.

02:30.890 --> 02:31.620
I am leaving.

02:33.770 --> 02:34.410
Do your best!

02:35.700 --> 02:37.150
Satoshi has won his way up.

02:37.960 --> 02:40.920
So I cannot afford to lose until I fulfill my promise with him.

02:41.720 --> 02:43.420
Come on, come on, hurry! Hurry!

02:43.990 --> 02:45.270
Let's go do some interviews!

02:47.440 --> 02:51.940
Interview, interview... We're always rushing around like crazy.

02:52.280 --> 02:57.880
Right. We have no time to get any of valuable Pokémon they have here at the Kalos League at all.

02:58.170 --> 03:02.430
Get them? We don't even have time to <i>appraise</i> them.

03:02.700 --> 03:05.190
Pikachu is right there, and yet...

03:07.270 --> 03:08.970
It's so irritating.

03:10.180 --> 03:12.430
The victory goes to Louis!

03:12.860 --> 03:16.020
With that, three semifinalists have been determined!

03:16.300 --> 03:19.310
There is only one bracket left!

03:21.220 --> 03:21.930
Guys!

03:23.750 --> 03:24.640
Did I make it in time?

03:25.310 --> 03:25.900
Sana!

03:26.430 --> 03:27.250
You have made it.

03:27.800 --> 03:29.390
Tierno's match is starting now.

03:30.030 --> 03:30.590
Thank goodness.

03:31.330 --> 03:33.230
Serena, it's been a while! Have you been doing all right?

03:33.530 --> 03:35.760
Yeah. I'm glad you seem to be doing well too, Sana.

03:36.070 --> 03:37.360
Yeah, I am!

03:37.720 --> 03:38.410
What about Satoshi?

03:38.800 --> 03:40.600
He's already advanced to the semifinals.

03:41.470 --> 03:42.610
Oh, it's you, Sana!

03:43.190 --> 03:45.900
Yo! I heard you made it to the next round, Satoshi.

03:46.430 --> 03:46.760
Yeah.

03:47.150 --> 03:48.700
Hey, who's Tierno's opponent?

03:49.430 --> 03:51.160
A Trainer named Shota.

03:51.790 --> 03:53.070
Shota is strong.

03:53.750 --> 03:55.410
I've lost to him once.

03:55.950 --> 03:56.110
What?

03:56.820 --> 03:57.910
Is he <i>that</i> strong?

03:58.300 --> 04:01.500
He is not only strong, but a hard worker and a good analyst.

04:01.500 --> 04:03.420
This will be a tough fight.

04:05.090 --> 04:08.050
The last battle of the Kalos League quarterfinals is...

04:09.210 --> 04:10.450
...Tierno...

04:10.650 --> 04:12.470
...against Shota!

04:13.100 --> 04:15.110
And this will be the field:

04:16.850 --> 04:18.740
The badlands field!

04:24.350 --> 04:25.360
Both of you, please call out your Pokémon.

04:25.990 --> 04:27.680
Please come out, Gillgard!

04:30.990 --> 04:31.560
That is...

04:33.950 --> 04:36.470
Gillgard, the evolved form of Nidangill.

04:36.860 --> 04:42.980
It can detect the innate qualities of leadership. According to legend, whoever it recognizes is destined to become king.

04:43.500 --> 04:45.210
So Nidangill has evolved.

04:45.640 --> 04:49.760
What Pokémon will Tierno counter this with?

04:50.280 --> 04:53.510
Runpappa, it's dancing time!

04:56.200 --> 04:58.530
Turn! One, two, three, step!

04:58.530 --> 05:00.320
One, two, three, four!

04:59.480 --> 05:03.090
Wow, Runpappa has started dancing! That's what they're known for!

05:05.220 --> 05:06.510
I expected nothing less from Tierno.

05:06.870 --> 05:09.070
And he is perfectly in sync with Runpappa, too.

05:09.680 --> 05:10.950
Do your best, Shota!

05:11.230 --> 05:12.620
Do your best, Tierno!

05:14.960 --> 05:16.530
Have a good battle, you two.

05:17.100 --> 05:18.660
Begin the match!

05:27.860 --> 05:30.250
We'll come at you with our rhythm!

05:30.690 --> 05:32.340
Runpappa, Rain Dance!

05:42.910 --> 05:43.680
Rain Dance...

05:44.270 --> 05:46.960
So he went and raised the power of its Water type moves.

05:47.550 --> 05:48.920
That is in accordance with theory.

05:49.620 --> 05:50.530
In that case, we will do the same.

05:51.000 --> 05:52.670
Gillgard, Swords Dance!

06:00.610 --> 06:03.210
So his strategy is to raise its Attack power with Swords Dance, huh...?

06:04.270 --> 06:08.980
Tierno used Rain Dance to use the field to his advantage, while Shota placed weight on one single, upcoming hit.

06:09.960 --> 06:11.590
I wonder who will be declared the winner.

06:12.670 --> 06:14.070
Use Swords Dance once more!

06:14.350 --> 06:15.630
Runpappa, Hydro Pump!

06:19.090 --> 06:19.410
It is fast!

06:21.470 --> 06:24.080
I see... Runpappa's Ability is Swift Swim.

06:24.650 --> 06:28.860
Rain Dance not only raised the power of its Water type moves, but also its speed.

06:30.030 --> 06:30.890
He is good.

06:31.770 --> 06:33.290
Don't give them any time to rest! Hydro Pump!

06:35.210 --> 06:35.860
Slash!

06:40.760 --> 06:42.000
Are you all right, Gillgard?

06:43.020 --> 06:46.340
Yo! Yo, yo! Are Yo giving up or what?!

06:47.430 --> 06:51.470
Runpappa is using its speed and power to toy around with Gillgard!

06:55.350 --> 06:57.110
Its power and speed...

06:57.620 --> 06:58.840
...are making this slightly troublesome.

06:59.370 --> 07:02.420
Tierno's Runpappa is well raised.

07:03.130 --> 07:05.050
He is making good use of Rain Dance.

07:05.660 --> 07:07.810
I wonder how Shota will overcome this.

07:09.110 --> 07:09.690
In that case...

07:10.280 --> 07:11.900
Use Hydro Pump once more!

07:13.340 --> 07:13.930
Gillgard,

07:14.190 --> 07:14.860
King's Shield!

07:21.190 --> 07:22.490
Gillgard's stance...

07:22.880 --> 07:23.500
...has changed.

07:30.900 --> 07:34.910
King's Shield allows it to change into its Shield Forme, which protects it from attacks,

07:35.340 --> 07:37.890
and sometimes even lowers the opponent's Attack power.

07:40.220 --> 07:41.510
King's Shield, huh...?

07:42.570 --> 07:43.820
It is time to counterattack.

07:44.190 --> 07:46.180
Gillgard, use Sacred Sword!

07:50.990 --> 07:51.770
Hydro Pump!

07:59.530 --> 07:59.810
What?!

08:00.260 --> 08:01.320
Now, use Swords Dance!

08:08.540 --> 08:09.000
Runpappa,

08:09.330 --> 08:10.390
Solar Beam!

08:14.590 --> 08:15.990
Use Sacred Sword once more!

08:27.800 --> 08:28.730
Runpappa!

08:29.280 --> 08:30.630
Runpappa is unable to battle!

08:31.680 --> 08:32.730
Gillgard wins!

08:33.450 --> 08:35.210
It's settled!

08:35.630 --> 08:39.470
Gillgard has slashed through Solar Beam and claimed a brilliant victory!

08:39.660 --> 08:42.030
Shota claims the first victory!

08:43.400 --> 08:44.540
Thank you, Runpappa.

08:46.180 --> 08:47.260
Take a long rest.

08:50.080 --> 08:53.330
Raichu, it's dancing time!

09:04.890 --> 09:06.010
Pokémon Quiz.

09:06.210 --> 09:07.210
The answer is...?

09:09.010 --> 09:18.960
Coming up next:

09:09.010 --> 09:13.980
Raichu VS Jukain!!

09:09.890 --> 09:14.640
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

09:14.020 --> 09:18.960
Shota has a surprising secret plan!!

09:27.480 --> 09:29.120
Raichu, Charge Beam!

09:32.770 --> 09:33.590
King's Shield!

09:40.640 --> 09:42.180
King's Shield again, huh?

09:42.600 --> 09:44.360
Now, Gillgard! Slash!

09:47.560 --> 09:48.370
Dig!

09:51.110 --> 09:51.660
Good job!

09:54.860 --> 09:58.210
Tierno's Raichu has dodged the move brilliantly by using Dig!

09:59.730 --> 10:00.740
Gillgard, here it comes!

10:05.380 --> 10:06.210
All right!

10:09.240 --> 10:10.090
Gillgard!

10:11.820 --> 10:12.840
Gillgard is unable to battle.

10:13.610 --> 10:14.850
Raichu wins!

10:19.330 --> 10:20.110
All right!

10:20.500 --> 10:22.840
Raichu, let's keep this rhythm!

10:26.690 --> 10:27.940
Thank you, Gillgard.

10:28.560 --> 10:29.730
Please take a long rest.

10:30.300 --> 10:31.550
Now it is one-to-one.

10:32.040 --> 10:33.270
They're both good.

10:33.800 --> 10:35.750
My heart won't stop pounding!

10:35.750 --> 10:37.780
I wonder what Pokémon he'll call out next.

10:38.440 --> 10:42.740
Geez, I'm exhausted. We do one interview after another with no end in sight.

10:43.210 --> 10:45.250
I don't want to hear the words "Pokémon League of Fierce Fights"...

10:45.570 --> 10:47.330
...ever again!

10:47.660 --> 10:50.600
If I hear them one more time, I'll scream!

10:50.600 --> 10:51.290
Same.

10:52.080 --> 10:57.050
Hey, in that case... Why don't we quit this job and concentrate on getting Pokémon?

10:57.360 --> 10:57.770
You're right.

10:58.100 --> 10:59.770
Let's just run off!

11:00.100 --> 11:00.580
Hey!

11:00.910 --> 11:02.540
Don't rest; <i>move</i>!

11:02.820 --> 11:04.830
All right, let's go continue with our coverage!

11:04.830 --> 11:06.340
The Pokémon League of Fierce Fights!

11:09.300 --> 11:10.690
Peroream, Attract!

11:22.180 --> 11:22.870
Raichu!

11:23.340 --> 11:28.090
Uh-oh! Tierno's Raichu has become infatuated with Peroream!

11:28.660 --> 11:30.300
Raichu, Charge Beam!

11:35.290 --> 11:36.920
Aw, geez!

11:37.330 --> 11:38.630
Peroream, Energy Ball!

11:45.640 --> 11:46.720
Raichu...

11:49.630 --> 11:50.520
Return for now!

11:51.990 --> 11:53.790
Unable to put up with it, Raichu has been returned!

11:54.550 --> 11:55.410
Kamex,

11:56.380 --> 11:57.110
I'm counting on you!

12:03.510 --> 12:05.160
There you are, Kamex.

12:05.730 --> 12:07.310
Peroream, Attract!

12:10.030 --> 12:12.380
Kamex, it's dancing time!

12:17.800 --> 12:18.580
I see.

12:18.870 --> 12:19.880
So it does not work.

12:20.430 --> 12:21.740
There's nothing to be surprised about.

12:22.080 --> 12:24.890
After all, we're already Attracted to dancing!

12:26.780 --> 12:29.140
Tierno and Kamex are amazing!

12:30.000 --> 12:32.310
Citron, is that even possible?

12:32.310 --> 12:34.860
The mental aspect may be a factor,

12:35.240 --> 12:38.290
but it is probably just because they are both male.

12:38.290 --> 12:39.170
Thought so.

12:39.480 --> 12:41.990
Kamex, Hydro Cannon!

12:44.710 --> 12:45.970
Peroream, please dodge!

12:53.340 --> 12:54.060
Peroream!

12:55.150 --> 12:56.750
Peroream is unable to battle!

12:57.160 --> 12:58.260
Kamex wins!

12:58.780 --> 13:00.120
All right!

13:03.220 --> 13:04.240
Thank you very much.

13:04.640 --> 13:05.640
Please take a long rest.

13:06.970 --> 13:07.800
I have got one left.

13:08.930 --> 13:09.930
I will place my bets on you!

13:10.410 --> 13:12.200
Please come out, Jukain!

13:15.550 --> 13:18.200
That Jukain sure has some good movements.

13:18.640 --> 13:19.690
All right, Kamex!

13:20.030 --> 13:21.740
Ice Beam!

13:24.510 --> 13:25.280
Leaf Storm!

13:31.160 --> 13:31.900
I've got to hand it to them.

13:32.310 --> 13:33.330
This won't be easy.

13:34.120 --> 13:35.590
Hydro Cannon!

13:36.920 --> 13:38.040
Dodge and use Leaf Blade!

13:45.980 --> 13:46.770
Kamex!

13:52.420 --> 13:54.650
That Jukain really is nimble...

13:55.210 --> 13:57.630
But my Kamex has more power!

13:58.000 --> 13:59.510
Go! Skull Bash!

14:03.220 --> 14:04.950
Jukain, Frenzy Plant!

14:10.270 --> 14:11.070
Kamex!

14:12.360 --> 14:12.910
Use Rain Dance!

14:23.960 --> 14:24.700
Rain Dance?

14:25.120 --> 14:25.720
Why?

14:31.370 --> 14:32.720
Kamex is unable to battle!

14:33.690 --> 14:34.710
Jukain wins!

14:35.830 --> 14:36.510
Kamex,

14:36.890 --> 14:38.090
thanks for all you did.

14:41.950 --> 14:44.350
That was a cool Rain Dance that paved the way to our next move.

14:45.110 --> 14:45.810
Come out,

14:47.400 --> 14:48.060
Raichu!

14:51.340 --> 14:53.500
The last matchup is Jukain VS Raichu!

14:54.280 --> 14:56.020
In terms of power, Jukain is superior.

14:56.620 --> 14:57.040
However,

14:57.640 --> 14:58.580
something bothers me.

14:59.320 --> 15:01.450
I wonder why he used Rain Dance at the end.

15:04.160 --> 15:07.420
Who will proceed to the semifinals? Will it be the Shota...

15:07.700 --> 15:09.550
...or Tierno?

15:10.210 --> 15:10.800
Raichu,

15:11.290 --> 15:12.050
Thunder!

15:12.580 --> 15:15.400
I see! When its rains, Electric moves are sure to hit!

15:15.740 --> 15:17.770
They never miss.

15:17.770 --> 15:19.520
So that's why Kamex used Rain Dance...

15:22.640 --> 15:24.120
All the battles we have had so far,

15:24.480 --> 15:25.690
all the EXP we have gained...

15:26.050 --> 15:27.670
They are our strength!

15:34.010 --> 15:36.410
Jukain, mega evolve!

15:57.540 --> 15:59.440
Jukain mega evolved!

15:59.900 --> 16:01.400
So that's Shota's secret weapon...

16:01.700 --> 16:03.100
Mega Evolution, you say?

16:03.400 --> 16:04.250
So that's how you want to play.

16:04.760 --> 16:05.440
Raichu, go!

16:17.600 --> 16:18.350
It's not working?!

16:18.710 --> 16:22.020
Raichu's full force strike was prevented by Lightning Rod!

16:22.480 --> 16:26.460
When Jukain mega evolves, its Ability changes to Lightning Rod.

16:27.150 --> 16:28.620
Thunder will not work.

16:28.930 --> 16:29.800
No way...

16:30.780 --> 16:32.140
Jukain, Dragon Claw!

16:34.820 --> 16:35.430
Raichu,

16:35.690 --> 16:36.740
Focus Blast!

16:48.450 --> 16:49.290
Raichu!

16:55.940 --> 16:57.260
Raichu is unable to battle.

16:57.590 --> 16:59.720
Therefore, the winner is Shota!

17:10.610 --> 17:11.940
It's over for us.

17:13.470 --> 17:14.720
Let's root for the winner.

17:15.210 --> 17:16.830
Aw, Tierno...

17:16.830 --> 17:20.230
I guess Shota's desire to win was just a little bit stronger.

17:20.740 --> 17:23.810
That may have made the difference between victory and defeat.

17:25.080 --> 17:25.580
Really though,

17:26.100 --> 17:28.090
to think that Jukain mega evolved...

17:30.890 --> 17:33.170
Shota has prepared for the Kalos League, too.

17:34.030 --> 17:35.490
I'm looking forward to fighting him.

17:37.220 --> 17:39.930
We've now got all the semifinalists!

17:40.300 --> 17:44.120
From the semifinals on, we will finally have full six-on-six battles!

17:44.600 --> 17:46.810
This are the brackets!

17:49.390 --> 17:51.030
Alan against Louis...

17:51.650 --> 17:53.780
...and Satoshi against Shota!

17:54.360 --> 17:58.780
Tomorrow will also see fierce battles, as the Kalos League continues on!

18:05.800 --> 18:06.360
Satoshi,

18:06.710 --> 18:09.270
there will be full battles next; what is your strategy?

18:09.700 --> 18:09.920
Huh?

18:10.570 --> 18:13.490
You only have five Pokémon; what are you going to do about your last one?

18:14.170 --> 18:15.740
Oh! What time is it right now?

18:17.510 --> 18:18.020
Oh, darn it!

18:18.900 --> 18:19.960
What's wrong?

18:20.190 --> 18:20.990
Satoshi!

18:25.370 --> 18:27.330
They should be coming soon...

18:28.390 --> 18:29.430
"Coming"? Who?

18:32.550 --> 18:33.180
There they are!

18:36.000 --> 18:36.760
Numelgon!

18:41.550 --> 18:43.270
Thank you so much, Kenzo-san.

18:43.860 --> 18:44.980
It was no trouble at all.

18:48.120 --> 18:48.920
Numelgon!

18:49.390 --> 18:50.980
So your last one will be...

18:51.640 --> 18:53.440
Yeah... My last one...

18:54.120 --> 18:54.920
...is Numelgon!

18:57.880 --> 19:00.120
The truth is, I decided on this from the very beginning.

19:00.600 --> 19:01.690
Ever since we dropped by that place.

19:07.340 --> 19:08.700
It's finally time for the Kalos League.

19:10.880 --> 19:14.050
Apparently, once you win your way up, there will be six-on-six battles.

19:14.490 --> 19:16.510
But I only have five Pokémon on hand right now.

19:17.420 --> 19:20.050
I've considered having Professor Okido send someone to me,

19:20.680 --> 19:23.670
but there's someone else I really want to battle alongside.

19:29.400 --> 19:31.110
And that's you, Numelgon.

19:32.370 --> 19:34.140
Please fight together with me at the Kalos League.

19:41.590 --> 19:44.230
Stop it! You're hurting me, Numelgon!

19:54.420 --> 19:57.720
I won't be able to win the Kalos League if I don't fight together with you guys.

19:58.510 --> 20:00.050
This is my best team!

20:00.830 --> 20:03.560
Let's all make sure to win against Shota!

20:06.390 --> 20:11.070
After they welcomed Numelgon, Satoshi and his Pokémon will fight in the upcoming semifinals.

20:11.900 --> 20:14.030
His opponent will be none other than Shota.

20:15.430 --> 20:17.960
The time to fulfill their promise has finally come.

20:27.430 --> 20:28.670
Hey, everyone!

20:27.620 --> 20:30.240
Professor Okido

20:31.510 --> 20:33.330
The Pokémon I'll be introducing today is...

20:34.460 --> 20:38.880
Volcanion
Species: Steam Pokémon
Type: Fire/Water
Height:1.m
Weight: 195.0kg
Ability: Water Absorb

20:34.630 --> 20:38.240
...Volcanion, who'll also be playing a huge role in the movie that premieres next week.

20:38.880 --> 21:10.830
Premieres Saturday July 16th

20:39.270 --> 20:43.740
Volcanion is a mythical Pokémon said to live in remote mountains.

20:44.110 --> 20:44.280
Huh?

20:45.610 --> 20:46.550
Yo, human.

20:46.880 --> 20:48.590
How many times're ya gonna crash into me before yer satisfied?

20:48.760 --> 20:54.370
It lives hidden from humans, releasing a mist of steam from the arms on its back.

20:55.160 --> 20:57.740
Volcanion is a Fire/Water type.

20:58.150 --> 21:00.530
One of the moves it can use is Steam Eruption.

21:00.920 --> 21:04.360
It is said to be so powerful that it can blast away mountains.

21:08.440 --> 21:09.410
Get blown away!

21:11.040 --> 21:15.480
The special pre-order ticket with which you can obtain Volcanion will only be on sale until July 15th.

21:15.810 --> 21:16.450
Hurry!

21:17.080 --> 21:21.000
Premieres Saturday July 16th

21:17.730 --> 21:20.370
Everyone, get Volcanion!

21:21.000 --> 21:26.010
Sunday July 10th at 8am!

21:22.040 --> 21:23.580
Let's go to the theater!

21:24.280 --> 21:25.630
On Sundays at 8am!

21:26.900 --> 21:29.090
A 2-hour Pokémon Movie Special!

21:29.880 --> 21:33.020
The big battles between legends from last year's blockbuster,

21:33.670 --> 21:37.580
"The Archdjinni of Rings: Hoopa", will finally be broadcast on TV for the first time!

21:38.470 --> 21:41.940
The short movie that was a big sensation, "Pikachu and the Pokémon Musicians",

21:41.940 --> 21:43.010
will be on air as well!

21:44.260 --> 21:47.300
Also, there will be lots of never before shown footage of the newest movie,

21:48.060 --> 21:52.060
"Volcanion and the Ingenious Magearna", showing intense battles and intense emotion!

21:52.830 --> 21:54.990
On Thursday the 14th, at 6pm!

21:55.940 --> 22:00.880
Next week we have a 2-hour Pokémon Movie Special

21:56.730 --> 22:01.360
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:00.920 --> 22:06.030
The world premiere of The Archdjinni of Rings: Hoopa
